  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building daycare center in Phum Brammouy, Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodia, garment factories employ nearly 700,000 people, approximately 90% of whom are women. These women have the dual burden of caring for their children and providing income for their families. As a result, some women leave their children in their home villages to work in urban areas, or they leave their children with family, friends or other caregivers all day, six days per week to work.</narrative>
  </description>
